v2.2.0 stopped the hooks assuming `node` — `hooks/lib/json.sh` tries node, then python3, then jq; the three git gates fail CLOSED with none of them and the fail-open hooks warn once — added an optional `**Protected branches**:` field, and fixed the bootstrap path end to end (dry-run placeholder report, `--build-cmd`…`--default-branch` on every variant, `--wrap-existing-claude-md`, recursive `hooks/` copy in PowerShell, whole-line `.gitignore` merge, the inline-comment gitignore bug, the dead SQLite placeholders). v2.2.1 fixes the same node assumption in `scripts/test-hooks.sh` itself: its payload builders were `node -e` one-liners, so on a node-less host every payload was empty and the suite reported 128 failures that were all the harness. Builders are printf + a sed escaper now (no interpreter at all), the six node-only hook blocks SKIP instead of failing, and the suite is green with node hidden. Also: the `none` merge semantics are stated with a field-verified matrix, `agent-budget-warn.sh` documents that it is parser-free by construction, and the hook-testing docs name the fresh-TMPDIR rule for WARN cases. 12 hook scripts + `hooks/lib/`, 8 skills; 230 consistency assertions, 269 hook fixtures.
